<% content_for :title, "There is a problem with this person's account – Digital Prison Services" %>

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
    <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">
      There is a problem with this person's account
    </h1>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      This person's account may not be set up correctly or they may no longer have access to this service.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">
      What you need to do
    </h2>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">
      Check their access roles
    </h3>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      Ask a local systems administrator to confirm the user has been given the Allocations - POM role on Digital Prison
      Services.
    </p>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">
      Ensure they have been added to this service
    </h3>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      Go to the <%= link_to 'Manage staff section', prison_poms_path(@prison.code), class: 'govuk-link' %> to see if
      this person is listed as either a prison POM or probation POM. If not,
      <%= link_to 'add them as a POM', search_prison_onboarding_index_path(@prison.code), class: 'govuk-link' %>.
    </p>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">
      Check the Attention needed tab
    </h3>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      If they are listed on the Attention needed tab of
      the <%= link_to 'Manage staff section', prison_poms_path(@prison.code), class: 'govuk-link' %>, you must
      reallocate their cases so they can be removed from this service.
    </p>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">
      Change their status
    </h3>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      If this person has left the prison either permanently or temporarily, select their name in
      the <%= link_to 'Manage staff section', prison_poms_path(@prison.code), class: 'govuk-link' %> and then select
      edit profile to change their status.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
